---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Colophon"
  description="How this site is built, styled, and kept private."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Colophon</p>
    <h1>How this site works</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Astro</strong> — static site generator; builds plain HTML/CSS from Markdown.</li>
      <li><strong>Markdown + Git</strong> — every post is a file in the repo. Writing and site history live together.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> — hosting and auto-deploy on push.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Design</h2>
    <p>
      Dark, technical theme with system fonts (no webfont downloads) and monospace
      used for metadata. The accent color is a restrained sky blue. No client-side
      JavaScript frameworks; the only script on the page is Astro's build output,
      which is effectively none.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      There are no trackers, no cookies, no analytics, and no third-party embeds.
      The site is static files: whatever the host logs server-side is out of my
      control, but nothing is collected or rendered into the page itself.
    </p>

    <h2>Writing a post</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Copy a template from <code>templates/</code> into <code>src/content/writing/&lt;category&gt;/</code>.</li>
      <li>Fill in the frontmatter (<code>title</code>, <code>date</code>, <code>category</code>) and write.</li>
      <li>Set <code>draft: false</code> when it's ready to publish.</li>
      <li>Commit and push — the site rebuilds automatically.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      To add a new category, create a folder under
      <code>src/content/writing/</code> and add a title/description to
      <code>src/data/categories.ts</code>. That's it — category pages and feeds
      appear automatically.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
